{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>יורא</b> — from the language of והורית להם (Exodus 18:20). The meaning: the soul that gives of its blessings, HaShem will fatten it, and HaShem will multiply [that with] which he waters it." "<b>גם הוא יורא</b> — and He commanded to water a man who lacks, and this is: הענק תעניק לו והחזקת בו (Deuteronomy 15:14)." "Another interpretation: ומרוה is joined with נפש ברכה. The meaning: a man who waters — גם הוא יורא — in the sense of fattening, for he is fattened by watering a man who lacks. Another interpretation: the sage who waters others — El will give him authority."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:22:14.498227288Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}